  "caption": "Quinn is on week nine of rehab: same three exercises, same weight, and a pain score that changes every day. Is it even working?\n\nRecovery is rarely a straight line. Function can improve before pain does, and exercises usually need to get gradually harder to keep driving change.\n\nSome ways to judge it: track two or three measures (like walking time, reps or load, and a weekly pain average), review every two weeks rather than daily, notice quieter wins such as shorter bad days and better sleep, and ask your clinician for a clear progression plan.\n\nIf nothing has shifted after a genuine 6–8 weeks, or you notice new numbness, weakness or spreading pain, a review is a good idea.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
